    "sourcePrompt": "Three-column time-echo split effect over backgroundVideo. Default state: full-width single video playing normally. THREE times during this 30-second clip the frame splits into three equal vertical columns showing the same video at three time offsets. The split exits only when a scene cut is detected in the video\nSPLIT ENTER — 3 fixed trigger times\nt=3.0s, t=12.0s, t=22.0s\nEnter animation: 0.15s easeOut. Two black bars (10px wide) slide in simultaneously — left bar translateX(-100%)→0 anchored at 33.33% of frame width; right bar translateX(+100%)→0 anchored at 66.67%. #splitLayer fades opacity 0→1 over 0.15s. Full-width single video fades opacity 1→0 over 0.15s\nSPLIT HOLD — time-echo columns\nThree absolutely-positioned column wrappers inside #splitLayer, each overflow:hidden\nLeft col (left:0, width:33.33%): video element, src=backgroundVideo, currentTime = masterTime\nCenter col (left:33.33%, width:33.34%): separate video element, same src, currentTime = masterTime + 0.3s\nRight col (left:66.67%, width:33.33%): separate video element, same src, currentTime = masterTime + 0.6s\nEach video is 100vw wide, positioned left:0 / left:-100vw / left:-200vw respectively so only the correct third is visible inside its clipping wrapper. Sync center and right on every requestAnimationFrame: centerVid.currentTime = leftVid.currentTime + 0.3; rightVid.currentTime = leftVid.currentTime + 0.6. Clamp to video duration. All video elements muted\nSCENE-CUT DETECTION for EXIT\nHidden offscreen canvas 64×36px sampling leftVid each rAF while split is active\n1. Draw leftVid frame to canvas\n2. getImageData, compute average luminance (sum R+G+B of all pixels / (3 × pixelCount))\n3. If |currentLuminance - prevLuminance| > 18, declare scene cut → trigger EXIT\n4. Safety fallback: if split held > 4.0s with no cut detected, trigger EXIT anyway\nSPLIT EXIT — scene cut detected OR 4s fallback\n0.15s easeIn. Single CSS transition on #splitLayer only: opacity 1→0. NO per-column or per-bar stagger. Simultaneously: left bar translateX(0)→translateX(-100%), right bar translateX(0)→translateX(+100%), both 0.15s easeIn. Full-width single video fades opacity 0→1 over 0.15s. After exit completes, stop detection loop until next trigger\nBETWEEN EVENTS\n#splitLayer: visibility:hidden, opacity:0. Full-width backgroundVideo: opacity:1, playing. No artifacts\nDIVIDER BARS (children of #splitLayer, inherit parent opacity)\nTwo divs inside #splitLayer. Width:10px, height:100%, background:#000000, position:absolute\nLeft bar: left:calc(33.33% - 5px). Right bar: left:calc(66.67% - 5px)\nbox-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.45). z-index above column videos\nNo text, no captions, no labels, no UI chrome. Pure geometric temporal split on a serene matte pastel ancient Chinese landscape video",
